{"kind":"promise","text":"I will make the narrow repair on request/kernel-cache-orchestration and nothing else.\n\nTwo edits: delete gitstore.Store.CommitTree, whose last two production callers this change removed, and rewrite the CommitMessageWithTimestamp comment so it describes what that function is actually for now — the oracle two tests measure the new normalization against — instead of claiming event scans call it for a per-commit process saving they no longer take.\n\nI will not touch the unification itself. I reviewed it and found it sound; a repair that drifts into the thing it was repairing is how a narrow change stops being reviewable.\n\nOne thing I will check rather than assume: TestVerifierRejectsCommitTreeDifferentFromSignedPayloadTree names CommitTree but tests the verifier's rejection of a commit whose tree differs from the signed payload tree. That behaviour is still enforced, through commit.Tree rather than a CommitTree call, so I expect the test to stay and only its dependency to change. I will confirm that before deleting anything.\n\nI will carry current main, which has advanced to b84d698d since the reviewed head, commit with this request trailer, and run the full gate set: focused gitstore and kernel, race, vet, build, full suite, and git diff --check. Then replacement exact-head artifacts and a fresh independent review, which has to be codex's — I found this blocker, so I cannot also be the one who judges the fix.","body":{"branch":"request/kernel-cache-orchestration"}}